
How to setup backend:

1. Setup python virtual environment. I used anaconda, but whatever works.
2. Install requirements.txt
    - For anaconda, the command was """conda install --yes --file requirements.txt"""

3. To start server, run the command """python manage.py runserver"""
    - By default, the server will start at """http://127.0.0.1:8000/"""

Bonus - """http://127.0.0.1:8000/test/""" will give you a simple http response
